              "np.float64(0.04626531069684985)"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 134
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "standard_error = np.std(sample_means)\n",
        "standard_error"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "74b99ef2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "74b99ef2"
      },
      "source": [
        "In this case, the standard error is about 0.045 kg -- so if we collect many samples, we expect the sample means to vary by about 0.045 kg, on average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "dc5be37f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dc5be37f"
      },
      "source": [
        "People often confuse standard error and standard deviation. Remember:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Standard deviation quantifies variation in measurements.\n",
        "\n",
        "* Standard error quantifies the precision of an estimate.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this dataset, the standard deviation of penguin weights is about 0.38 kg for chinstrap penguins."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 135,
      "id": "8254b93c",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-16T17:42:04.320899Z",
